r or violence and then  things obviously got out of control  protesters and the family attorney ben  crump say it was the officer who  escalated the situation some of the  community that we spoke to last night  said police need not only more  de-escalation training but also more  mental health and diversity training now  this officer is on paid administrative  leave while the michigan state police  investigates the incident then the kent  county prosecutor will look at the  findings from that investigation to  determine if any charges are warranted  gail  adriana what have we heard from mr  leoyea's family  gail we spoke to them yesterday and  the family is broken the mother was  crying throughout the press conference  we sat down with the family afterwards  and this family moved to the u.s from  the democratic republic of congo in 2014  they fled war there they're refugees and  the father told us we left  our country to come to america for  safety and he said he cannot imagine  that this has happened here he said my  son was killed like an animal the family  wants prosecutors to charge this officer  to the fullest extent of the law gail  all right adriana diaz reporting thank  you
 

